 - Change: strip leading zone prefixes before comparing screen lines, so initial frames, differential redraws, and history caches stay clean. Fullscreen behavior is unchanged.
 - Evidence: `test/unit/tui-engine-local-deltas.test.ts` checks initial and differential writes.
 - Removal condition: the selected Pi baseline supplies equivalent normal-mode filtering.
+
+## L035: Fullscreen scrollbar track interaction
+
+- Product contract: the fullscreen transcript is the product's primary scrollable surface, and MCode enables the Engine's dormant `ScrollView` scrollbar for it through the existing `scrollbar: "always"` option in the product-owned `chat-layout.ts`. A one-column, thumb-only press target makes the painted bar practically ungrabbable in real terminals, so the Engine contract Pi exposes is not operable as-is.
+- Minimal difference: `tui-alt-screen.ts` widens the scrollbar press hit target to a three-column span ending at the painted bar column and covering the full track height, and factors the existing drag mapping into `dragScrollbarTo`; a press on the empty track centers the thumb under the pointer before dragging, while a press on the thumb keeps the classic in-place grab. `components/scroll-view.ts` and `layout.ts` stay at the Pi baseline.
+- User impact: the always-on fullscreen transcript scrollbar can be grabbed, dragged, and clicked to jump; pointer presses on the thumb do not move content until dragged.
+- Evidence: `test/unit/tui-scrollbar-interaction.test.ts` feeds real SGR mouse press, motion, and release sequences through VirtualTerminal and asserts which content lines the viewport shows after track jumps, thumb grabs, and drags; the existing engine local-delta and Chat layout suites cover unchanged selection and layout behavior.
+- Removal condition: the selected Pi baseline provides an equivalent wide, track-clickable scrollbar interaction contract for product-enabled scroll views and MCode migrates to it.
